motion.prompt_template:
{kling_prompt}

This is a faceless cinematic journey in a fixed five-beat format. Honor the camera mode of this scene. SCENES 1-3 FIRST-PERSON POV (battered body-cam/handheld). Scene 1: BODY-CAM on a panicked sprinting runner — EXTREME body-cam vibration (head bob, strap wobble, gear bouncing, lateral shifts, sharp judders, irregular stumble-recovers, NO two consecutive frames alike, camera in all axes), water/lens splash/blur (wet) or dust/lens flare (dry), natural raw amateur texture, WORLD RUSHES PAST at sprint speed (~6–7 m/s), per-stride SURGE-AND-SETTLE, 3–4 strides/sec, frame rotation 8–15°/stride, panicked panting breath, door dominant focal point, brief 1–2 shoulder-glances backward, forearms occasionally at bottom of frame (not exaggerated), AND at the end the runner's HAND THRUSTS forward into the bottom-center of the frame and SHOVES the door open INWARD — door yields INWARD instantly under the VISIBLE HAND push (NOT auto-opening) — CAMERA PASSES THROUGH the doorway in CONTINUOUS FORWARD MOTION (NO recoil, NO pushed-back, NO bouncing) — runner ARRIVES at the TOP of the staircase — clip ends with camera AT THE TOP, ANGLED DOWNWARD at the DESCENDING steps that DOMINATE the frame. Scene 2: POV continuous descent first half — top to mid-descent, camera STAYS POV angled DOWNWARD, per-step bob downward, PROMINENT AUDIBLE footsteps on the SPECIFIC stair material (DOMINANT audio). Scene 3: POV continuous descent second half + arrival — mid-descent to bottom, same POV camera angled DOWN, PROMINENT AUDIBLE footsteps, and at the end the camera transitions from looking-DOWN-at-steps to LEVEL — at the FLOOR LEVEL of the lower room, looking AHEAD into the warm luxury interior. SCENES 4-5 OFF-POV THIRD-PERSON: calm controlled motion. Scene 4: slow horizontal lateral tracking shot across the lower room while the traveler walks IN the room in ONE consistent forward direction (NOT on the staircase). Scene 5: smooth continuous follow from behind into another luxurious room.

Keep the locked structure identity. The descent is always a normal short straight step staircase going DOWN, structurally attached — never floating, never ascending. K1 = top angled DOWN. K2 = mid-descent angled DOWN. K3 = at the bottom camera LEVEL with lower room ahead. The audio is natural diegetic sound only — wind/sea/rain + HARD pounding footsteps + panicked panting (S1, + hand-on-door slam and door creak at end), PROMINENT AUDIBLE footsteps on the SPECIFIC stair material (S2 and S3, dominant audio), calm walking footsteps in the lower room (S4-S5) — absolutely NO music. Every clip must depict ONE continuous motion from start to end — no time jumps, no mid-clip cuts, no skipping, no camera pushed back by the door.
